  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "2d0b22418501b5b545854e4335c4ff82627431d6",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 452820257,
          "type": null,
          "body": "@martin.r.mathieson there is another warning :\n\nepan/dissectors/packet-mysql.c:1547 proto_tree_add_item called for hf_mysql_max_packet  -  item type is FT_UINT24 but c                                                                                         all has len 4\nbut it is valid for both, there is a ignore list somewhere ?",
          "author": {
            "id": 279822,
            "username": "alagoutte",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Alexis La Goutte",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a15cba6417f4d1723eb56add7099bcfd8df373dc520577958b33c37915ef231b?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/alagoutte"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-11-23T15:19:03.127Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-11-23T15:19:03.127Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 79146057,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 1005,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "9d3941da6ea41f6acee6b0099a60a177dafd2a8e",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 452850725,
          "type": null,
          "body": "We could have a set of exceptions - see already known_non_contiguous_fields, which is a set of fields known to have valid non-contiguous bitmaks (usually multiple reserved fields with significant fields in between).\n\nIn this case, it is used for both lengths 3 and 4.  Would FT_UINT32 not be better then?  Can the length ever be > 2^24?  Presumably they wouldn't have widened the field if it could not?\n\nThe script doesn't warn if the length in the call is less than the width of the field.  It could be reworked to note all of the lengths used in calls for a field and make this clearer.  It's still probably a bug if any of the calls are for more than the width of the field though.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/030414c33f619ee28811cd9c073802ef2267d160ab2744eb8427bd49af4c7998?s=80&d=identicon",
